{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we first need to understand the geometry of the set \\(\\cal S\\). Set \\(\\cal S\\) consists of all line segments of length 2 whose endpoints lie on adjacent sides of a square with side length 2. Let's place the square in the coordinate plane with vertices at \\((0,0)\\), \\((2,0)\\), \\((2,2)\\), and \\((0,2)\\).\n\nConsider a line segment with endpoints \\((x,0)\\) and \\((2,y)\\). The length of this segment is 2, so we have:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(2-x)^2 + y^2} = 2\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\n(2-x)^2 + y^2 = 4\n\\]\nThis is the equation of a circle with center \\((2,0)\\) and radius 2. Similarly, for a line segment with endpoints \\((x,2)\\) and \\((0,y)\\), we have:\n\\[\nx^2 + (2-y)^2 = 4\n\\]\nThis is the equation of a circle with center \\((0,2)\\) and radius 2. The midpoints of these line segments will lie on the circle with center \\((1,1)\\) and radius 1, which is the intersection of the two circles.\n\n","prefix_end":903,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1156,1184,311,3535,279,17047,315,279,738,1124,11520,5416,328,59,568,2573,1124,11520,5416,328,57758,17167,315,678,1555,20632,315,3084,220,17,6693,36342,10246,389,23942,11067,315,264,9334,448,3108,3084,220,17,13,6771,594,1992,279,9334,304,279,16184,11031,448,17228,518,1124,1188,15,11,15,10699,701,1124,1188,17,11,15,10699,701,1124,1188,17,11,17,10699,701,323,1124,1188,15,11,17,10699,3593,37175,264,1555,10238,448,36342,1124,1188,87,11,15,10699,8,323,1124,1188,17,7358,10699,568,576,3084,315,419,10238,374,220,17,11,773,582,614,510,59,9640,59,26888,96065,17,6558,29776,17,488,379,61,17,92,284,220,17,198,59,921,50,446,3249,2176,11067,11,582,633,510,59,9640,7,17,6558,29776,17,488,379,61,17,284,220,19,198,59,921,1986,374,279,23606,315,264,12671,448,4126,1124,1188,17,11,15,10699,8,323,10578,220,17,13,34239,11